Here are the exact find-and-replace steps to fix the month capitalization and add the "(Execution time lapsed)" warning!
### 1. Fix the Month Capitalization Universally
The reason your months were lowercase is because .toLowerCase() was attached to your date formatter, forcing "Jun" to become "jun".
**Find this near the top of your file (around line 140):**
```javascript
const formatDateTime = (dateVal) => {
  if (!dateVal) return "N/A";
  // Formats to: "19 Jun 2026, 12:58 pm"
  return dayjs(dateVal).format("DD MMM YYYY, hh:mm a").toLowerCase();
};

```
**Replace with:**
```javascript
const formatDateTime = (dateVal) => {
  if (!dateVal) return "N/A";
  // Removing .toLowerCase() keeps DayJS's native capitalized months (e.g. 'Jun')
  return dayjs(dateVal).format("DD MMM YYYY, hh:mm a"); 
};

```
